// @@@ The index of the last occurrence of an element in the list is not -1, for all indices i where the index is greater than the last occurrence and less than the size of the list, the element at index i in the list is either null or not equal to the specified element.

--------------------
// @@@ The index of the last occurrence of an object in the list is not -1. For all indices i where the index is greater than the last occurrence and less than the size of the list, if the element at index i is null and the object o is not null, or if the element at index i is not null and not equal to o, then the condition holds.

--------------------
// @@@ For every index i where the last index of a certain object o is less than i and i is less than the size of the list, if the object o is null, then the element at index i in the list should be null. If the object o is not null, then the element at index i in the list should not be equal to o.

